# Auto-launches the Quill daemon (as a systemd --user unit, see
# quill-daemon.service) whenever a Samsung Android device is plugged in over
# USB in its normal MTP mode -- i.e. before the daemon's own AOA handshake
# switches it into accessory mode. Vendor ID 04e8 is Samsung's, not specific
# to any one device (S9 FE+, S10 FE+, etc. should all match).
#
# SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS reaches into the logged-in graphical session's systemd
# --user instance from udev's root context -- the standard mechanism for
# this (used by e.g. game controllers, docks), rather than a fragile
# su/DISPLAY-guessing shell script. Requires the unit to exist at
# ~/.config/systemd/user/quill-daemon.service and the user session to
# already be active (or lingering enabled).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="04e8", ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="quill-daemon.service", TAG+="systemd"
